    <string name="precise_location_info">Overcast works with your approximate location. If you allow precise location, it\'s used only to pinpoint the weather, radar and wind for exactly where you are, for example when your city spans several forecast areas.\n\nYour location is checked only when the weather refreshes. It\'s sent as coordinates to the weather and radar providers you\'ve chosen, and to Open-Meteo once per place to pick the landscape behind the sky. Overcast never keeps it on a server of its own, shares it with anyone else, or uses it for ads.\n\nYou can switch back to approximate location at any time in the system app settings.</string>
